From 61ac4f0ab47a304b94635ebe425d7b9ebc792f93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:54:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] feat(mailbox): add DKIM signing, inbound SPF/DKIM/DMARC
 and server hardening

Builds on the integrated mailbox server to replace the external
postfix/dovecot/opendkim container, so a Gitea instance can host its own
mail without a separate MTA.

Sender authentication:
- sign outbound mail with DKIM (RSA PKCS#1/PKCS#8, Ed25519 PKCS#8) across
  the webmail, authenticated submission and the [mailer] queue paths, so
  local and relayed copies carry the same signature
- authenticate inbound Internet mail with SPF, DKIM and DMARC, record the
  outcome in Authentication-Results, and honour the published policy:
  reject on p=reject, file into Junk on p=quarantine, defer on tempfail
- quarantined mail is kept out of the tokenized reply-by-email handler so
  it cannot mutate an issue or pull request

Wiring the feature into the tree:
- break the services/mailer -> services/mailbox -> services/auth import
  cycle by injecting the password authenticator from routers/init
- resolve a builder.Cond assignment, two untyped authres constants and two
  non-constant format strings that failed the build and go vet
- go mod tidy, which also records the whois dependency that
  modules/setting/blockers.go already imported

SMTP intake hardening:
- read command and DATA lines through a bounded reader; the previous
  length check ran after bufio had already buffered the whole line, so a
  peer that never sent a newline could exhaust memory on port 25
- strip one leading dot from every DATA line per RFC 5321 4.5.2 rather
  than only from lines starting with two dots
- remove exactly one line terminator instead of trimming every trailing
  CR and LF, which altered the bytes DKIM hashes

Recipient resolution:
- match the account name before aliases so an account registered after a
  colliding alias cannot have its mail delivered to the alias owner
- add POSTMASTER_USER for the RFC 2142 postmaster and abuse addresses,
  and CATCH_ALL_USER for the postfix catch-all behaviour; both default to
  empty, which keeps rejecting unknown recipients

IMAP and web list no longer load every raw message blob to list a folder;
the wire bytes are fetched only for the commands that need them.

Also localizes the webmail templates, documents every [mailbox] setting in
app.example.ini, and covers DKIM sign/verify round trips, DMARC alignment,
SMTP path parsing and DATA transparency with unit tests.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
